message.content:
Surgical fix for HOW IT WORKS section in /Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Marketing Site/Boldteq.

ROOT CAUSE (verified): Source image files Rectangle-243.png, Rectangle-244.png, Rectangle-186.png are 1492×1724 PORTRAIT on disk. Webflow markup uses `<img width="1492">` with no height attr. Webflow CDN serves a CROPPED 1492×840 LANDSCAPE variant via srcset. Local Next.js loads the full portrait file = renders 884px taller per image at mobile.

THE FIX:

1. File `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Marketing Site/Boldteq/src/components/home/how-it-works.tsx`:
   - Verify all 3 STEPS items have `imageHeight: 840` (NOT 1724). If currently 1724, change to 840.
   - The Image component already has `width={step.imageWidth} height={step.imageHeight}` and `sizes="(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 33vw"`. Don't change that.
   - Do NOT add inline style props.

2. File `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Marketing Site/Boldteq/src/components/home/how-it-works.module.css`:
   - Locate the `.fullWidthImage` rule (currently has `display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 3768px; height: auto`).
   - REPLACE with:
     ```
     .fullWidthImage {
       display: block;
       width: 100%;
       max-width: 100%;
       height: auto;
       aspect-ratio: 1492 / 840;
       object-fit: cover;
       object-position: top;
     }
     ```
   - Remove any other `.fullWidthImage` rules at min-width 1280/1440 that override `max-width` to 100% (already there) — keep the other padding/font rules in those breakpoints intact.

3. Build: run `pnpm build`. Must pass 0 errors.

CONSTRAINTS:
- TypeScript strict, no `any`
- Don't touch other files
- Don't run tests yourself
- Don't add deps

EXPECTED OUTCOME: Image displays as 1492:840 landscape rectangle with portrait source clipped from bottom. At 375 viewport with 100vw image = 375px wide × (840/1492) = ~211px tall. 3 cards × (211 image + ~80 text + padding) = ~870px total — close to live's 840px.

OUTPUT: 1-line summary of edit per file + build result.

